<Site title="Privacy" description="How Counted handles address searches, site requests and analytics."><div class="page-top page-share-heading"><h1>Privacy</h1><PageShare/></div><section class="card"><h2>Place and address search</h2><p>Using place or address suggestions anywhere on the site sends your search text and browser information to Google Maps Platform. Google’s <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> applies to that service.</p><p>Counted also receives your typed search and optional area scope to find official municipalities, districts and wards. These requests use POST, are not cached or saved to our datasets, and do not put your text in a public search URL.</p><p>When you select a province, town or other area, Counted receives its selected name, area type, province and representative coordinates to match our results directory. This request is not cached or saved to our datasets.</p><p>When you select an address or landmark, your browser sends its coordinates to Counted to find the electoral ward. Our lookup does not save your address, selected place or coordinates. They are not added to our public datasets. The selected place stays in this page until you leave or choose another location. The Explore map page saves its visible map position and selected electoral area in the page URL, so copying that link shares the map view. It does not include your address text or Google place ID.</p><h2>Election chat</h2><p>Questions sent through Ask Counted, recent messages in that conversation and the public data needed to answer them are sent to OpenRouter and the model provider it routes to. Their privacy and retention policies apply. Counted requests providers that do not collect prompts for training. Please do not include personal or sensitive information.</p><p>Counted saves conversations, partial answers, charts, progress updates and citations on Cloudflare so you can reopen them or reconnect while an answer is running. Anyone with a conversation link can read it. These links are not listed publicly or intended for search indexing. Starting a new chat does not delete an old one. Conversations currently have no automatic expiry. Your browser stores recent conversation links and a separate key that allows you to send or stop messages; that key is not included in share links. Clearing browser storage removes your ability to write to those conversations. Counted does not log transcript contents. To limit costs and abuse, we keep request counts with a daily, keyed hash of your network address; these counters are removed after their short retention period when chat is next used. Chat news research sends a search query to OpenAI’s native web search through OpenRouter. Search queries, retrieved material and source citations are processed by those providers under their policies. Research summaries and citations are saved as part of the publicly viewable conversation; Counted does not reuse them as a shared news cache. Public results charts and their source data may also be cached, without your question or conversation.</p><p>Chat citations display site icons from Google’s favicon service. Your browser requests these using the linked site’s hostname, without the article path, your question or a chat-page referrer. Google receives the icon request and normal connection information.</p><h2>Analytics</h2><p>We use Google Analytics to understand visits, popular pages and use of the site. It uses cookies to distinguish visits and processes information such as the pages viewed, referring website, browser, device and approximate location. We also measure use of sharing controls, including opening the share dialog, sharing, saving an image, copying a link or caption, format changes and errors. These events include the public page path and action type, but not the caption, image contents or selected coalition parties. We disable Google signals and advertising personalisation. We remove query strings and URL fragments from page addresses and referrers sent to Analytics, and disable search, form and map-history tracking so typed searches, address selections and precise map coordinates are not collected by those features.</p><p>Google’s <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how it processes data. You can block Analytics using your browser settings or Google’s <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</p><h2>Site requests</h2><p>Our hosting provider processes network requests to deliver the site and protect it from abuse. Avoid entering sensitive information in public search URLs. Election results and geographic boundaries are public data.</p></section></Site>
